        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French Minister visits Algeria amid diplomatic thaw Africa Issued on: 18/05/2026 - 16:47 Modified: 18/05/2026 - 16:50 France's justice minister Gérald Darmanin is in Algeria to discuss improving cooperation and the fate of a detained French journalist. The visit is a sign of warming ties between the two countries, after a diplomatic spat triggered among other things by Paris's official backing Moroccan sovereignty over the disputed Western Sahara region. For Darmanin, the goal is also to improve judicial cooperation between the two countries. ‘High time to push peace agenda’: Ebola outbreak in DRC spreads in conflict-hit, hard-to-reach areas 18/05/2026 Africa Nigeria: Who was the targeted Islamic State group leader and why was he targeted by the US? 18/05/2026 Africa Hantavirus cruise ship arrives in the Netherlands to be disinfected 18/05/2026 Europe France & Africa partnering on jobs, education, investment: 'Not just about money, also the diaspora' 18/05/2026 Africa France hopes for cooperation with Algeria to tackle DZ Mafia criminal organisation 18/05/2026 France DR Congo takes emergency measures to contain new Ebola outbreak 18/05/2026 Africa 18/05/2026 Europe 'Tool of control to crush dissent': Amnesty warns of global 'resurgence' in use of death penalty 18/05/2026 Middle East Ukraine strikes Russia: Zelensky says response to Moscow's agression 'justified' 17/05/2026 Europe"
