        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran sets up new Strait of Hormuz managing body amid stalled talks with US Middle East Issued on: 18/05/2026 - 16:33 Iran has formed a new body to manage the Strait of Hormuz. It comes as peace talks with the United States appeared to remain stalled. It's not clear what the new body will do, but earlier this month Iranian media said vessels seeking transit would have to apply to it for a permit - disclosing ownership, insurance, crew, and cargo. G7 finance ministers meet amid Middle East war economic fallout 18/05/2026 Middle East Israeli attacks in Gaza have stepped up since halt in bombing in Iran 18/05/2026 Middle East UAE nuclear power plant targeted in likely-Iranian attack 18/05/2026 Middle East War against Iran is \"growing more unpopular by the day\" in the US 18/05/2026 Americas 'Tool of control to crush dissent': Amnesty warns of global 'resurgence' in use of death penalty 18/05/2026 Middle East Drone hits UAE nuclear power plant: IAEA reports normal radiation levels 17/05/2026 Middle East Middle East: Israel attacks south Lebanon day after ceasefire extension 17/05/2026 Middle East Gaza flotilla sails for a third time despite threats: 500 activists depart 16/05/2026 Middle East 'No sign' of China's willingness to pressure Iran after Trump's visit 16/05/2026 Middle East"
